all right the American Embassy in Turkey  was shot at overnight at a time when  tensions are rising between turkey in  the u.s. local police are looking for  the suspects who opened fire early this  morning in the capital of Ankara the  Embassy was closed at the time of the  attack a spokesman for Turkey's  president says the gunmen wanted to  create chaos Holly Williams is an  Istanbul following the investigation  Holly good morning good morning the  authorities in Ankara say six rounds  were fired at the US Embassy at 5:30  this morning local time  from a white vehicle this is certainly  not the first time that a US diplomatic  mission here in Turkey has come under  attack in 2013 the Embassy was targeted  by a suicide bomber killing a security  guard and in 2015 attackers opened fire  outside the US consulate here in  Istanbul but this attack comes as  relations between the u.s. and Turkey to  NATO allies are strained perhaps even to  breaking point they are at odds over  several issues including pasta Andrew  Brunson an evangelical pastor from North  Carolina who Turkey accuses of spying  and terrorism and who's been in  detention here for nearly two years in  response the u.s. imposed sanctions this  month and both sides have imposed  announced tariffs on some goods Turkey's  president rejected Iran has called this  an economic war but we do not know if or  how this shooting was connected with  those tensions John Holly Williams in  Turkey thanks
 

